Finally got it working…

**STiRoT** leaves SAES in a state that retains the shared **RNG** path, causing `PKA_SR.INITOK` to remain 0 because, as described in [RM0481](https://www.st.com/resource/en/reference_manual/rm0481-stm32h523533xx-stm32h543553xx-stm32h562xx-and-stm32h563573xx-armbased-32bit-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf), `INITOK` stays low while **SAES** is using the **RNG** bus.

Resetting **SAES** in the secure application before the non-secure handoff fixed it:

```

__HAL_RCC_SAES_CLK_ENABLE();

__HAL_RCC_SAES_FORCE_RESET();

__DSB();

__HAL_RCC_SAES_RELEASE_RESET();

__DSB();

```

**PKA** now initializes normally in `IROT_PROVISIONED`.
